  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Sports Hall Floor",
    "overview": "The admin app is a calm pale floor (birch ground) with a deep Hallenblau rail along the left. Structure comes from lines: 1px hairlines separate rows, sections and sheet parts, and each group owns one court-line colour that appears as a short 2px stroke, never as a filled box. One signal orange-red, taken from the handball line, marks primary actions, focus and the current selection. Nothing else on the screen is that colour.\n\nThe density is set for the work: tables with 44px rows at 14px, the page title large at top left with a one-line summary under it, and the table directly beneath. Detail opens in a side sheet from the right, so the list stays put. Editing happens in place. Cmd/Ctrl+K opens a command palette from anywhere. Copy is German and uses \"Du\".\n\nRejected: a coloured header bar over grey cards and modal stacks (the easyVerein anti-reference), plus the banned generic tells listed under Don'ts.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Pale ground, white surfaces only where data lives (tables, sheets, inputs, portal cards).",
      "Lines carry structure; there are no card shadows.",
      "Group colour always appears as a short court line next to its name.",
      "One accent, used only for action, focus and current position.",
      "Display face for headings and headline figures, text face for everything else.",
      "Keyboard-first: palette, inline edit, row actions on hover and focus."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Signal Rule",
        "body": "The accent marks action, focus and \"you are here\". If it is not clickable, focused, selected or current, it is not accent.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Line-Not-Fill Rule",
        "body": "Court colours are drawn as lines (2-3px strokes, a 2px inset underline, a 2px left bar), always next to a text label. Never a filled chip or tinted card.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Column Rule",
        "body": "Body text keeps proportional figures (`'tnum' 0` on body). Numbers that align or compare (money and number columns, dates in timelines and court-line labels, headline figures) switch on tabular numerals and money columns align right.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Caps Rule",
        "body": "No uppercase labels and no tracked-out small caps anywhere; hierarchy comes from size, weight and colour.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Floor-Is-Flat Rule",
        "body": "Tables, cards, banners and buttons never carry a shadow. If it sits on the floor, it is outlined with a 1px hairline.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do take every colour, size, space and duration from `tokens.css`; new group colours get a `--court-*` token.",
      "Do keep the accent for primary action, focus, selection and current position.",
      "Do draw group and calendar colour as a short line next to its name.",
      "Do open detail and edit flows in the right side sheet or inline; keep the list visible.",
      "Do right-align money and number columns with tabular numerals.",
      "Do show row actions on hover and focus-within, never hide them from keyboard users.",
      "Do keep text at 15px for body and 13px as the floor for meta; keep the 2px accent focus outline on every interactive element.",
      "Do give controls 44px on coarse pointers and in the portal.",
      "Do write German UI copy with \"Du\"; label demo data with the yellow demo banner.",
      "Do zero all motion under `prefers-reduced-motion` (already global)."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add a coloured header bar over grey cards, or stack modals (the easyVerein anti-reference).",
      "Don't use a centred hero with a gradient blob, three identical cards, glassmorphism, purple gradients, or rounded-2xl with shadow-lg.",
      "Don't put shadows on tables, cards, buttons or banners.",
      "Don't exceed 4px radius on controls and containers.",
      "Don't fill chips or cards with a group colour.",
      "Don't use uppercase eyebrow or kicker labels above headings.",
      "Don't use emoji or text glyphs as icons; icons are Lucide SVGs at 14-18px.",
      "Don't load third-party fonts, trackers or CDNs; fonts ship through @fontsource.",
      "Don't invent stats or testimonials; overview figures are live counts.",
      "Don't let colour carry meaning alone; pair every status and court colour with text."
    ]
  }
